TITLE = "An Explainable Framework for Authenticity Screening of Images, Videos and Documents with Cross-Generator Evaluation"
KEYWORDS = "deepfake detection, AI-generated images, document tamper localization, cross-generator generalization, probability calibration, CLIP"

ABSTRACT = (
    "Fake pictures, manipulated face videos and altered documents come from different tools and leave different traces, yet the person who receives "
    "such a file needs a single answer that can be understood. This paper presents a framework that routes an uploaded image, video or document to a "
    "specialised analyser and turns the evidence into a calibrated 0&ndash;100 Trust Score, a three-band verdict and a short explanation. "
    "The image analyser is implemented and evaluated. It scores 224&times;224 patches of the original-resolution image with a frozen CLIP ViT-L/14 encoder and a "
    "logistic classifier that we trained on about 30,000 real and AI-generated images, using a randomly compressed copy of every training image. "
    f"On held-out generators ({n_real:,} real and {n_fake:,} AI images) it reaches an AUC of {A['test_clean']['auc']:.3f} (95% CI {ci('test_clean')}) on clean files and "
    f"{A['test_jpeg70']['auc']:.3f} after JPEG quality 70, and it catches {pct(gen('v3', 'gpt-image-1.5')[1])}% of GPT-Image-1.5 and {pct(gen('v3', 'nano-banana-pro')[1])}% of Nano Banana Pro images; "
    f"a variant trained without any OpenAI or Google image still catches {pct(gen('v3_proof', 'gpt-image-1.5')[1])}% and {pct(gen('v3_proof', 'nano-banana-pro')[1])}% of them. "
    "The video analyser (face crops from sampled frames, aggregation of frame scores, a timeline) and the document analyser (OCR, error-level, noise and DCT views "
    "feeding a dual-stream U-Net, plus arithmetic and PDF-structure checks) are specified together with their evaluation protocols. They have not been evaluated yet, "
    "so no results are claimed for them."
)

